      "abstract": "<p>\n                    We consider a Laurent series defined by the infinite product\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g Subscript u Baseline left-parenthesis t right-parenthesis equals product Underscript n equals 0 Overscript normal infinity Endscripts left-parenthesis 1 plus u t Superscript minus 2 Super Superscript n Superscript Baseline right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>g</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:munderover>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ∏\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                ∞\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                            </mml:munderover>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>+</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  −\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:msup>\n                                  <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                                  <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                                </mml:msup>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_u(t) = \\prod _{n=0}^\\infty (1 + ut^{-2^n})</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    , where\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"u element-of double-struck upper F\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ∈\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\in \\mathbb {F}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is a parameter and\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"double-struck upper F\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb {F}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is a field. We show that for all\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"u element-of double-struck upper Q minus StartSet negative 1 comma 0 comma 1 EndSet\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ∈\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Q</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo class=\"MJX-variant\">\n                              ∖\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              −\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\in \\mathbb {Q}\\setminus \\{-1,0,1\\}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    the series\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g Subscript u Baseline left-parenthesis t right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>g</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_u(t)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    does not satisfy the\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -adic Littlewood conjecture. On the other hand, if\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"double-struck upper F\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb {F}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is finite then\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g Subscript u Baseline left-parenthesis t right-parenthesis element-of double-struck upper F left-parenthesis left-parenthesis t Superscript negative 1 Baseline right-parenthesis right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>g</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>u</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ∈\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  −\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_u(t)\\in \\mathbb {F}((t^{-1}))</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is either rational or it satisfies the\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -adic Littlewood conjecture.\n                  </p>",
